2026-09-23 — bounded private-leaf substitution and complete inline values.

RED: zero Rust compilation errors; 1 declared leaf-call shape failure, 3
controls PASS. Further explicit-always_inline reductions fail on the prior
release independently of the new cost model: inline-value-transport.c has a
foreign SSA Value ID after its second builtin operand opens a block;
inline-complex-parameter.c reports E3101 for a synthetic scalar destination.

GREEN: use the existing C-HIR substitution for private leaves of at most 48
nodes, excluding calls, loops, local objects, exposed objects, assembly, label
identity, statement expressions, constant queries, activation-sensitive
builtins and optimization barriers anywhere in the declaration chain. Existing
address/alias/reference retention and variadic boundaries still apply. There
is no new IR rule, source admission or EqSat allowlist expansion.

Floating builtin operands now retain earlier values in the explicit live
environment across later operands' control flow. Integer-complex parameters
use the ordinary pair-conversion node and checked StoreScalar initializer;
results use the parser's complete memory-place assignment and caller-owned
storage. Complex remains a C scalar, not an InitPlan CopyAggregate exception.
No validator, poison check or arithmetic obligation is weakened.

Five CLI regressions validate IR and both interpreters at O0/O2, cover
conversion/evaluation/read counts, unselected null reads, cost/admission
boundaries and retained E3001/E3002/E3004/E3009. The existing 63 language
semantic cases also pass. Four old call/body-inspection tests explicitly use
noinline to preserve what they inspect; their semantic assertions are intact.
The three C fixtures each exit zero with sealed GCC 14.2.0-19, Clang 19.1.7
and EvoCC at O0/O2: 18/18 native runs. All use linux/arm64, network none,
evo-flight-lab:sealed configuration digest
2c23684c9cc5ef5899073b59844fa47cc3c1d894f2316e21f25d5d85be5a10e2.

The unchanged arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/pgtable.o is replayed using its original
Kbuild command and actual bpf-config generated headers. Existing cmdrecord
projection records omitted options and forwards original assembler flags.
Old/new objects assemble with identical exported symbol names/types. Three
calls and the unused kvm_pgtable_walk_continue definition disappear; total
object text is 41688 -> 41816 bytes, data 1032 -> 1000 bytes. This is NOT a
runtime speedup measurement or original K03 PASS. No installed kernel object,
Image or module was changed. The original 120-second all-mode failure remains.

Affected gate against 1a2e98d: 1812 PASS, 0 FAIL, 3 historical ignored,
211 result groups across eight crates. Clippy --all-targets -D warnings,
workspace fmt --check and diff checks PASS. Initial failed gate retained
separately; the green gate is not a reinterpretation of that earlier failure.
The rebuilt release emits byte-identical original page-table assembly to the
tested debug compiler; no additional runtime acceptance is inferred.
Artifacts: .build/floating-targeted/private-leaf-20260923/ (about 10 MiB).
No clone, kernel rebuild or additional runtime disk was made.

